    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d815">

                <pb facs="1114" n="994" xml:id="pg994"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Treaty Series No. 668</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Costa Rican Minister for Foreign Affairs</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Coronado</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the American Minister</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-11-10"><hi rendition="#italic">November 10,
                        1922</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 333 B</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Minister</hi>: I have the honor to inform Your
                    Excellency that I have received instructions from the President of the Republic
                    to declare on the part of the Government of Costa Rica, with reference to the
                    extradition treaty that Your Excellency and the undersigned have just signed,
                    that it is understood that the Government of the United States of America gives
                    assurance that the death sentence will not be passed upon criminals surrendered
                    by Costa Rica to the United States of America for any one of the crimes
                    enumerated in the said treaty, and that that assurance will form an effective
                    part of the treaty and that it will be so mentioned in its ratification.</p>
                <p>I avail myself [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. A. Coronado</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
